<title>RUSSIA: Russian Sberbank hits $200 resistance.</title>
<headline>Russian Sberbank hits $200 resistance.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian savings bank Sberbank rose to $200 per share, hitting a psychological resistance level on sharp demand for the limited liquidity stock on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Sberbank shares, which were only recently listed on the Russian Trading System, was trading at $200.00 at 1129 GMT, after $196.50 at the close on Monday. Tuesday turnover was $2.7 million.</p>
<p>It closed at $143.90 on Monday June 1.</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
